.TH NVZ 1 "November 2026" "nvz 2.0" "User commands"
.SH NAME
nvz \- content-aware archiver that knows what it is packing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvz pack
.I dir archive.nv
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B nvz unpack
.I archive.nv target
.br
.B nvz list
.I archive.nv
.br
.B nvz test
.I dir
.br
.B nvz
.RI [ FLAG ]...
.RI [ FILE ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nvz
classifies its content and applies content-specific, lossless transforms —
deduplication, similarity sorting, PNG unfolding with recipe search,
lossless JPEG recoding and context-mixing compression — before choosing a
codec per block by probing a sample. Everything is bit-exact: every
transform is tried in both directions at pack time, and whatever cannot be
reproduced exactly is stored raw.
.PP
Five things
.B tar
does not do:
.TP
.B 1. Identical files are stored once.
Content is hashed with blake2b; duplicates become pointers into the same
block.
.TP
.B 2. Similar files are placed next to each other.
Entries are sorted by content class and extension before compression, so
the compressor's window sees likenesses that sat far apart in directory
order. Within a group, files larger than an eighth of the block cap go
first — the large file builds the dictionary the small ones match into.
.TP
.B 3. PNGs are unfolded and recompressed.
The IDAT stream is unfolded to raw filter rows, and the zlib recipe that
reproduces the original stream byte for byte is stored, together with a
fingerprint of the deflate engine that wrote it. On unpack every IDAT
chunk is verified against its CRC.
.TP
.B 4. JPEGs are recoded without touching a pixel.
The Huffman entropy layer is replaced by an adaptive arithmetic coder
(nvjpg); the DCT coefficients themselves are untouched and the original
bytes are proven reproducible before the transform is accepted.
.TP
.B 5. Nothing is assumed \(em everything is probed.
Each block chooses its codec by compressing a sample with every candidate:
zstd, xz with a dictionary that covers the block, or the context mixer
nvcm.
.SH SUBCOMMAND FLAGS
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " fast|normal|small|gpu"
.B small
(the default) is the smallest archive nvz can make;
.B normal
skips the most expensive re-checks and is the mode that beats the best
established tool on both size and time on most corpora;
.B fast
is deduplication and sorting with zstd \-3, matching a plain
\fBtar | zstd \-3\fR pipeline in speed.
.TP
.BI \-\-codec " zstd3|zstd19|zstd22|xz9e|nvcm|nvlz"
Force one codec instead of probing. Exists for measurements.
.TP
.B \-\-portable
Restrict the archive to the codecs {ra, xz9e, xz9e\-j0} and switch the
transforms off. Such an archive can be unpacked by the pure-stdlib Python
tool
.B portable/nvzpy.py
on macOS and Windows \(em no libzstd, no nvcm, no deflate-engine
dependency. Slower and somewhat larger; portability is the point.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dedup
Store every copy separately. Exists to measure what deduplication is worth.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-transform
Switch off the PNG and JPEG transforms.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sort
Leave objects in directory order. An ablation flag: it isolates what the
similarity sort \(em and only it \(em is worth; see
.B experiment/ablation.sh.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-classing
Put everything into one block stream instead of one block per content
class. Together with
.B \-\-no\-sort
this is nvz with no reordering at all, the comparison point against
.B tar
in directory order.
.TP
.BI \-\-block\-cap " MiB"
Raw bytes per block, default 192. The number of blocks governs the
parallelism (one block is compressed by one thread) and the ratio (one
block is the compressor's window), so this flag is the time/size dial.
Opaque blocks are exempt.
.TP
.BI \-j " N" "\fR, \fP" \-\-jobs " N"
Number of parallel jobs. Default is the number of threads, at most 24.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Say nothing.
.SH THE GZIP SURFACE
Without a subcommand,
.B nvz
behaves like
.BR gzip :
\fBnvz file\fR replaces the file with \fIfile\fR.nv (the archive inherits
its time and permissions), \fBnvz \-d\fR brings it back,
.B \-c \-k \-l \-t \-r \-S \-f \-v
and
.B \-1..\-9
mean what they mean in gzip. Two deliberate differences: the default level
is the SMALLEST, and a directory operand becomes ONE archive of the whole
tree, with the source tree always left in place.
.SH SWEDISH ALIASES
The tool was born Swedish, and published reports and scripts use the old
names. They are permanent aliases: the subcommands
.BR packa ", " packa\-upp ", " lista ", " prova ;
the flags
.BR \-\-läge ", " \-\-kodek ", " \-\-blocktak ", " \-\-jobb ", "
.BR \-\-utan\-dedup ", " \-\-utan\-omvandling ", " \-\-utan\-sortering ", "
.BR \-\-utan\-klassning ", " \-\-tyst ;
and the mode values
.BR snabb " (fast) and " liten " (small)."
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 all well, 1 error, 2 warning. One failing operand does not stop the
rest.
.SH FILES
Scratch space honors
.BR TMPDIR .
.SH NOTES
.TP
.B No special files.
Pipes, sockets and devices are skipped with a warning. Hard links are
recreated as independent files.
.TP
.B Standard input does not stream.
\fBcat file | nvz\fR works, but lands in a scratch file on the way: the
register sits at the end of the archive and is read first.
.TP
.B No encryption and no redundancy.
An archive with secrets should have mode 600; a flipped bit in a block
ruins the block \(em and is detected, never silently passed through.
.TP
.B PNG portability.
A PNG recipe depends on the deflate engine (zlib vs zlib-ng). The recipe
carries the engine's fingerprint; on a mismatch nvz searches the parameter
space and otherwise refuses with both fingerprints named. Use
.B \-\-portable
or
.B \-\-no\-transform
for archives that must open anywhere.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nvcm (1),
.BR nvjpg (1),
the measurement report in
